proposals.what:
This ports the bank's core power (a named misconception behind every wrong option, plus "another like this") to Reading & Writing words.

CONTENT: server/words/frames.json. Each frame is {id, key slug, sense, text, clue, needs, charge, subject}:
- text is 2–3 sentences with ____;
- clue is the [start,end] spans of the words that fix the meaning, e.g. "did not support";
- needs is the meaning the blank requires, in one line ("to weaken");
- charge is +, − or 0.
The spec's 1–3 `cloze` per SAT word become frames. The target is at least 2 per word, about 1,500 frames.

GENERATOR: a bank topic plug-in, satbank/topics/words_in_context/ (Topic.subject='rw', domain 'Craft and Structure'). It emits a normal Item through item.assemble_text, so each item is addressed by (frame, seed). The seed picks 3 distractors, and each distractor's reason is its trap:
- Opposite: from `opposite`;
- Lookalike: from lookalike confusions;
- Everyday meaning: for second_sense words, used in the "As used in the text, what does X most nearly mean?" form;
- Too strong / Too weak: from scales (proposal 6);
- Wrong charge: same subject, opposite connotation;
- Unrelated meaning: same part of speech and subject.
The reason text is one sentence, e.g. "Reverses the meaning: the text needs 'to weaken'; 'bolster' means to strengthen."

There are two SAT stems: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?" and "most nearly mean".

The audit re-derives the item. It checks:
- the key's sense equals `needs`;
- no distractor is in the key's `same` list, or one hop from it;
- the part of speech matches;
- there are at least 3 legal traps.

VERDICT (UI.workspace quiz mode):
- the key is amber and the pick is struck through;
- the .mistake line shows a mono trap tag and the sentence;
- the clue span is highlighted in wash with an amber underline, followed by "Clue: 'did not support' → the blank means 'to weaken'";
- all 4 options list their reason with no toggle.

After the verdict come two buttons:
- Same word, new text (key: A): another frame for that key;
- Same trap, new word (key: T): quiz_item(..., want_trap=kind) puts that trap kind among the distractors.

TRAP PROFILE: word_reviews gains a trap column. My words and every run summary show a bar list, e.g. "Your misses in context, 30 days: Everyday meaning 9 · Too strong 5 · Lookalike 3". Each row has Drill this trap: a 10-item run in which every item carries a distractor of that kind. The Status filter gains "Fell for a trap".

PACE: a per-item clock. The summary shows "Median 41 s · SAT pace 71 s" (32 min ÷ 27).

Because it is a bank plug-in, misses become normal traps: Review, the 3/10/30-day check-ins and mastery work unchanged. It is hidden from math tests, the coach and the math practice map by subject.

